1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,710
It is September eighteenth, two thousand one.

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:07,804
One week after the towers came down, sixteen acres of Lower Manhattan are still burning.

3
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:14,811
In Washington, the head of the Environmental Protection Agency puts out a statement about what the people down there are breathing.

4
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:21,001
It is one sentence long. Their air is safe to breathe, and their water is safe to drink.

5
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:26,887
Twenty five years later, that sentence is the most examined thing the agency has ever said.

6
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:35,269
Because two years after it was written, the agency's own internal watchdog looked at the data behind it, and found the data was not there yet.

7
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:42,669
And this week, after a court ordered it, New York City opened a filing cabinet it had kept shut for a quarter of a century.

8
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,769
This is a story about what officials said in the days after.

9
00:00:46,769 --> 00:00:50,481
About what their own watchdog later found they did not know when they said it.

10
00:00:50,481 --> 00:00:53,204
And about what the people who believed them are still paying.

11
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:56,828
Before we go further, one thing this is not.

12
00:00:56,828 --> 00:00:59,600
This is not a story about how the towers fell.

13
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,927
That question has an engineering answer, and we have already covered it.

14
00:01:04,066 --> 00:01:06,025
You're watching Black Box Breakdown.

15
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:10,405
The nine eleven files New York hid for twenty five years.

16
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:16,366
To understand the argument, you have to start with what was actually said, and when.

17
00:01:17,499 --> 00:01:21,198
September thirteenth, two thousand one. Two days after the attack.

18
00:01:21,198 --> 00:01:26,746
The Environmental Protection Agency issues its first public statement on the air over Lower Manhattan.

19
00:01:27,866 --> 00:01:30,073
September sixteenth. A second release goes out.

20
00:01:30,073 --> 00:01:36,695
It says the new samples confirm that ambient air quality meets Osha standards, and is not a cause for public concern.

21
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:40,995
September seventeenth. The New York Stock Exchange reopens.

22
00:01:40,995 --> 00:01:46,924
It has been closed for four trading days, the longest shutdown since nineteen thirty three.

23
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,523
September eighteenth. The sentence.

24
00:01:49,523 --> 00:01:54,257
Their air is safe to breathe, and their water is safe to drink.

25
00:01:55,399 --> 00:01:58,675
Read it in twenty twenty six and it sounds like a lie.

26
00:01:58,675 --> 00:02:02,223
Read it in September of two thousand one and it sounds like relief.

27
00:02:02,223 --> 00:02:05,771
That gap is the whole story, and it is worth being careful about.

28
00:02:06,899 --> 00:02:10,815
Because a statement being wrong, and a person lying, are two different findings.

29
00:02:10,815 --> 00:02:16,538
Only one of them has ever been established here. Hold on to that. We will come back to it.

30
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:20,670
So what was in the air over Lower Manhattan that September?

31
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:26,694
Two towers, a hundred and ten stories each, did not fall as buildings.

32
00:02:26,694 --> 00:02:28,200
They fell as powder.

33
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:32,719
Concrete, gypsum wallboard, and glass fiber, pulverized and thrown across the island.

34
00:02:33,866 --> 00:02:36,474
The United States Geological Survey went and sampled it.

35
00:02:36,474 --> 00:02:43,427
So did a team of environmental scientists led by Paul Lioy, whose work became the reference study on what that dust was made of.

36
00:02:44,566 --> 00:02:48,685
The finding that matters most is not any single poison. It is the alkalinity.

37
00:02:48,685 --> 00:02:52,509
The dust measured a pH between roughly nine and eleven and a half.

38
00:02:52,509 --> 00:02:56,922
Chemically, that is closer to drain cleaner than to anything a lung is built for.

39
00:02:58,066 --> 00:03:02,820
Responders had a name for what it did to them within days. The World Trade Center cough.

40
00:03:03,966 --> 00:03:11,143
On top of the caustic base: asbestos, from the fireproofing sprayed on the North Tower's lower floors.

41
00:03:11,143 --> 00:03:11,987
Lead. Dioxins.

42
00:03:11,987 --> 00:03:17,053
Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, thrown off by fires that burned for three months.

43
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:26,029
And the particles themselves were unusually large and unusually rough, which meant they lodged high in the airway instead of passing through.

44
00:03:26,029 --> 00:03:29,588
The dust was engineered, by accident, to stay in people.

45
00:03:30,733 --> 00:03:33,513
None of that chemistry mattered to anyone in September.

46
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:35,984
What mattered was who was standing in it.

47
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:43,611
About forty thousand people worked the pile and the surrounding zone over ten months.

48
00:03:43,611 --> 00:03:46,851
Firefighters, police, construction crews, sanitation workers, volunteers.

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:48,928
Respirators were available.

50
00:03:48,928 --> 00:03:54,191
Watch almost any archival footage of the site and you can see what actually happened with them.

51
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:57,238
Some crews wore them. Many did not.

52
00:03:57,238 --> 00:04:01,865
And a lot of the footage shows the same specific thing. The respirator is on the man.

53
00:04:01,865 --> 00:04:03,771
It is just not on his face.

54
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,431
There are ordinary reasons for that.

55
00:04:06,431 --> 00:04:12,048
The masks were hot, they fogged, they made it impossible to talk to the man next to you on a debris pile.

56
00:04:12,048 --> 00:04:16,133
And they were uncomfortable in a way that felt trivial next to what everyone was doing.

57
00:04:17,266 --> 00:04:20,613
And there was one more reason, which is the reason this episode exists.

58
00:04:20,613 --> 00:04:22,673
The government had said the air was safe.

59
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,710
It was not only the pile.

60
00:04:25,710 --> 00:04:30,487
Four blocks north, Stuyvesant High School reopened on the ninth of October, two thousand one.

61
00:04:31,633 --> 00:04:37,688
Students and parents were told the building had been cleaned, and that high efficiency air filters had been installed.

62
00:04:37,688 --> 00:04:39,600
Lila Nordstrom was a senior there.

63
00:04:40,733 --> 00:04:45,228
The filters had not been installed. The vents were later found still caked with dust.

64
00:04:45,228 --> 00:04:52,122
Nordstrom has spent the twenty five years since then organizing the students who sat under them, and she testified about it before Congress.

65
00:04:53,266 --> 00:04:54,231
Keep her in mind.

66
00:04:54,231 --> 00:04:59,535
She is going to appear again at the end of this, in a room nobody in two thousand one would have predicted.

67
00:05:00,666 --> 00:05:04,715
In two thousand three, somebody inside the agency went looking for the data.

68
00:05:05,833 --> 00:05:08,686
Every federal agency has an Office of Inspector General.

69
00:05:08,686 --> 00:05:11,222
It is internal, but it is deliberately independent.

70
00:05:11,222 --> 00:05:17,562
Its job is to investigate its own agency and publish what it finds, whether or not the agency likes it.

71
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:27,172
On August twenty first, two thousand three, that office published report number two thousand three, dash P, dash zero zero zero one two.

72
00:05:27,172 --> 00:05:33,067
A hundred and sixty five pages on how the agency handled the World Trade Center collapse.

73
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:38,798
The first thing it establishes is a timeline. Not of the attack. Of the sampling.

74
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:46,038
When the agency said the air was safe on September eighteenth, sampling for fine particulate matter had not started.

75
00:05:46,038 --> 00:05:49,572
It began on September twenty first. Three days after the sentence.

76
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:56,323
Data on polychlorinated biphenyls, on dioxin, and on those polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons was likewise incomplete.

77
00:05:56,323 --> 00:05:59,697
The watchdog's finding is narrow and it is devastating.

78
00:05:59,697 --> 00:06:04,571
The agency did not yet have the data to support what it said.

79
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:08,732
Be precise about what that does and does not mean.

80
00:06:08,732 --> 00:06:11,764
It is a finding about an institution and its evidence.

81
00:06:11,764 --> 00:06:16,616
It is not a finding that any individual knew the air was dangerous and said otherwise.

82
00:06:16,616 --> 00:06:19,649
The report makes no such finding, and neither will we.

83
00:06:20,766 --> 00:06:22,834
But the report was not finished.

84
00:06:22,834 --> 00:06:28,002
Because while the investigators were reconstructing how those statements got written, they found something else.

85
00:06:29,133 --> 00:06:32,842
The press releases did not go straight from the agency to the public.

86
00:06:33,966 --> 00:06:36,946
The report records an instruction sent to senior agency officials.

87
00:06:36,946 --> 00:06:42,012
All statements to the media should be cleared through the National Security Council before they are released.

88
00:06:43,133 --> 00:06:52,380
And per the agency's own Chief of Staff, one particular official at the White House Council on Environmental Quality was designated to work with the agency to make sure that clearance happened.

89
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,482
The report never names that person. Neither will this video.

90
00:06:56,482 --> 00:07:00,658
What the report documents is not who they were. It is what they changed.

91
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,007
Table two dash four.

92
00:07:03,007 --> 00:07:07,533
The draft of the September sixteenth release, printed beside the version that actually went out.

93
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:10,551
The report's own summary of it is one sentence long.

94
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:16,729
Quote. Every change that was suggested by the Council contact was made.

95
00:07:16,729 --> 00:07:21,339
The official's suggested changes added reassuring statements, and deleted cautionary statements.

96
00:07:22,466 --> 00:07:26,223
Here is the sentence that was deleted from the draft and not replaced.

97
00:07:26,223 --> 00:07:36,337
The concern raised by these samples would be for the workers at the cleanup site, and for those workers who might be returning to their offices on or near Water Street, on Monday, September seventeenth.

98
00:07:37,466 --> 00:07:42,207
That is a warning to two specific groups of people, on a named street, on a named day.

99
00:07:42,207 --> 00:07:46,948
It was written, and then it was taken out, and the people on that street went to work.

100
00:07:48,066 --> 00:07:49,160
Then the softening.

101
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:58,272
The draft read: seven debris and dust samples taken Thursday showed levels of asbestos ranging from two point one percent to three point three percent.

102
00:07:58,272 --> 00:08:03,374
The agency views a one percent level as the definition of asbestos containing material.

103
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:09,327
Here is what went out instead. Ranging from two point one to three point three.

104
00:08:09,327 --> 00:08:12,546
Slightly above the one percent trigger for defining asbestos material.

105
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:16,846
Two to three times a safety threshold is not slightly above it.

106
00:08:16,846 --> 00:08:19,230
That is the same number, wearing a different coat.

107
00:08:20,366 --> 00:08:22,863
And then there is the bottom of the table.

108
00:08:22,863 --> 00:08:27,303
A column of instructions from the White House office, printed next to the lines they produced.

109
00:08:27,303 --> 00:08:30,632
One of them is not a sentence. It is a stage direction.

110
00:08:31,766 --> 00:08:34,927
Quote. Insert Henshaw quote somewhere around here.

111
00:08:36,066 --> 00:08:41,119
And the line that appeared in the finished release, under the name of John Henshaw, Assistant Secretary of Labor.

112
00:08:41,119 --> 00:08:46,437
Our tests show that it is safe for New Yorkers to go back to work in New York's financial district.

113
00:08:47,566 --> 00:08:52,276
Be fair about what that shows. Press offices draft quotes for officials to approve.

114
00:08:52,276 --> 00:08:54,631
That is normal, if unlovely, government communication.

115
00:08:54,631 --> 00:09:01,359
There is no finding anywhere that Henshaw was deceived, or that he disagreed with the line issued under his name.

116
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:07,433
What is not normal is the direction of every single edit. Caution out. Reassurance in.

117
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:09,735
Not one change in the other direction.

118
00:09:10,866 --> 00:09:13,887
The report also records what was weighing on the messaging.

119
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,699
The desire to reopen Wall Street.

120
00:09:16,833 --> 00:09:24,461
And when the watchdog tried to establish exactly how those edits happened, and asked to sit down with the White House office that made them, it hit a wall.

121
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:25,926
Quote.

122
00:09:25,926 --> 00:09:31,477
Our analysis of the Council's input was limited, because Council officials chose not to meet with us.

123
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,645
That is not an allegation from a critic.

124
00:09:34,645 --> 00:09:41,038
That is a federal watchdog, in its own published report, recording that the office it was investigating would not sit in a room with it.

125
00:09:42,166 --> 00:09:46,999
For a long time, that report was the whole story. Then the bill started arriving.

126
00:09:48,133 --> 00:09:56,792
In two thousand ten, Congress passed the James Zadroga Nine Eleven Health and Compensation Act, signed into law on the second of January, two thousand eleven.

127
00:09:56,792 --> 00:10:01,455
It created a federal program to monitor and treat people exposed at the site.

128
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:08,167
It is named for a New York police detective who worked the pile and died in two thousand six.

129
00:10:08,167 --> 00:10:10,218
His own cause of death was contested.

130
00:10:10,218 --> 00:10:13,441
The city's Chief Medical Examiner attributed it to prescription drug misuse.

131
00:10:14,566 --> 00:10:20,964
Other pathologists, including a former Chief Medical Examiner of New York City, maintained the death was dust related.

132
00:10:20,964 --> 00:10:26,295
That dispute was never resolved, and it is worth saying plainly rather than smoothing over.

133
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:30,024
Here is what the program itself now reports.

134
00:10:30,024 --> 00:10:37,151
As of the thirtieth of June, twenty twenty six: a hundred and forty five thousand, two hundred and seventy five people enrolled.

135
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,854
Enrolled does not mean sick.

136
00:10:39,854 --> 00:10:44,828
That number counts people in monitoring, including residents and students with a wide range of exposure.

137
00:10:44,828 --> 00:10:47,626
The number that means sick is the next one.

138
00:10:48,766 --> 00:10:53,599
Sixty seven point three percent of them have been certified with at least one condition linked to the exposure.

139
00:10:54,733 --> 00:11:00,140
And fifty seven thousand and forty four people have had a cancer certified as linked to what they breathed.

140
00:11:01,266 --> 00:11:06,924
Twenty five years on, cancer is now the single most frequently newly certified condition in the program.

141
00:11:06,924 --> 00:11:10,252
The curve has not turned over. It is still climbing.

142
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:16,320
You will often hear it said that more people have now died from the dust than died on the day itself.

143
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:19,367
We are not going to say that, because nobody can actually support it.

144
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,597
The program reports deaths among its members from all causes.

145
00:11:23,597 --> 00:11:27,933
As of March of twenty twenty four, six thousand eight hundred and ninety seven.

146
00:11:27,933 --> 00:11:33,509
And it states, in its own words, that it does not track cause of death for deceased members.

147
00:11:34,633 --> 00:11:41,574
So there is no official figure to set against the two thousand seven hundred and fifty three killed at the site that morning.

148
00:11:41,574 --> 00:11:43,988
The honest version is smaller and still terrible.

149
00:11:43,988 --> 00:11:46,101
Fifty seven thousand certified cancers, and counting.

150
00:11:47,233 --> 00:11:50,080
Which brings us to a storage room, and to this week.

151
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,626
Everything so far came from the federal side.

152
00:11:53,626 --> 00:11:56,053
The agency investigated itself and published the result.

153
00:11:56,053 --> 00:12:00,604
The city of New York had its own records, and those had never come out.

154
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:08,002
In twenty twenty three, an advocacy group called Nine Eleven Health Watch filed public records requests with the city for them.

155
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:13,644
In January of twenty twenty four, the Department of Environmental Protection answered.

156
00:12:13,644 --> 00:12:15,899
It said no such records existed.

157
00:12:17,033 --> 00:12:21,317
In October of twenty twenty five, the department acknowledged about forty boxes.

158
00:12:22,466 --> 00:12:27,612
By November, it was sixty eight boxes. Roughly three hundred and forty thousand pages.

159
00:12:28,733 --> 00:12:37,249
On the twenty eighth of May, twenty twenty six, a New York Supreme Court justice ruled that the city's handling of those requests had been arbitrary and capricious.

160
00:12:38,366 --> 00:12:47,848
And on the eighth of September, twenty twenty six, three days before the twenty fifth anniversary, the city opened a public portal with the first hundred and seventy thousand pages on it.

161
00:12:48,966 --> 00:12:49,292
Now.

162
00:12:49,292 --> 00:12:55,810
It matters who is being held responsible here, and it is not one administration and it is not one party.

163
00:12:56,933 --> 00:13:00,062
Those boxes sat at that department through four mayors.

164
00:13:00,062 --> 00:13:03,190
A congressional request in twenty twenty one went unanswered.

165
00:13:03,190 --> 00:13:10,491
The requests that were actively denied, and the litigation that followed, happened under the administration in office from twenty twenty two.

166
00:13:11,633 --> 00:13:15,000
But only that last stretch carries an actual court finding.

167
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:23,754
The broader claim, that four administrations withheld these records, is the advocacy group's characterization, and it should be labeled as theirs rather than borrowed as ours.

168
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,472
And here is the part nobody has answered.

169
00:13:27,472 --> 00:13:33,259
How twenty thousand documents sat unlisted in a city department for two decades has never been publicly explained.

170
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,322
The department has declined to comment since November of twenty twenty five.

171
00:13:37,322 --> 00:13:41,949
We are not going to guess at the answer. We are just going to note that there isn't one.

172
00:13:43,066 --> 00:13:47,507
The people on the other end of this have answers, and they deserve to be heard in full.

173
00:13:48,633 --> 00:13:52,946
Rudy Giuliani, mayor at the time, responded to this month's release himself, publicly.

174
00:13:52,946 --> 00:13:58,586
His position is that the agency said the air was safe, and that nobody covered anything up.

175
00:13:59,733 --> 00:14:06,159
Christine Todd Whitman, who ran the Environmental Protection Agency and said the sentence, has addressed it more than once over the years.

176
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:11,249
In twenty sixteen she said this. I'm very sorry that people are sick.

177
00:14:11,249 --> 00:14:15,502
And if the agency and I in any way contributed to that, I'm sorry.

178
00:14:16,633 --> 00:14:19,536
And in the same breath she rejected the idea that she lied.

179
00:14:19,536 --> 00:14:23,164
We did the very best we could at the time, with the knowledge we had.

180
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:28,813
Both halves of that belong together, and you will often see only the first one quoted.

181
00:14:28,813 --> 00:14:34,174
It is an apology for an outcome, and a denial of intent, and she has been consistent about both.

182
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,719
People did sue her.

183
00:14:36,719 --> 00:14:41,334
Residents and workers brought federal claims arguing the reassurances themselves caused them harm.

184
00:14:42,466 --> 00:14:43,156
They lost.

185
00:14:43,156 --> 00:14:53,855
In Lombardi against Whitman, in two thousand seven, the appeals court affirmed dismissal, holding the conduct did not shock the conscience, which is the legal standard those claims had to clear.

186
00:14:55,000 --> 00:15:05,266
In Benzman against Whitman, the following year, the same court went further and reversed the one claim against her that a lower court had allowed to survive, sending it back with directions to dismiss.

187
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:10,680
So let's be exact, because this is the part the internet gets wrong in both directions.

188
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:15,229
No court has ever held her personally liable. And no court has ever found that she lied.

189
00:15:16,366 --> 00:15:20,224
What is established is narrower, and it is on the record in a federal report.

190
00:15:20,224 --> 00:15:22,282
The statement went out ahead of the data.

191
00:15:22,282 --> 00:15:26,397
And every edit made to the release before it went out ran in the same direction.

192
00:15:27,533 --> 00:15:31,369
Lila Nordstrom was seventeen when she was told her school building was clean.

193
00:15:31,369 --> 00:15:38,452
In June of twenty nineteen she was in a hearing room in Washington, testifying about what happened to the students who sat in it.

194
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:44,104
This month, when the boxes finally opened, reporters went back to her for comment.

195
00:15:44,104 --> 00:15:46,679
Twenty five years, to get to the paperwork.

196
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:51,840
What stays with me isn't the redline, or the stage direction in the margin.

197
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:52,994
It's that deleted sentence.

198
00:15:52,994 --> 00:15:59,921
Somebody wrote a warning for the people on Water Street, and somebody took it out, and on Monday morning those people went to work.

199
00:16:01,066 --> 00:16:07,022
There are still two hundred and seventy thousand pages in those boxes that nobody outside city government has read.

200
00:16:08,166 --> 00:16:17,281
If what a government put in writing about that day interests you, wait until you see what its own engineers concluded about the third building that fell, the one nobody was hit by.

201
00:16:17,281 --> 00:16:20,043
Watch our Building Seven investigation, right here on this channel.

202
00:16:20,043 --> 00:16:25,015
And subscribe to Black Box Breakdown, so you don't miss what the next set of documents turns up.

